      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I feel personally that the chatbox is flipped to how it should be\n\nInstead of choosing if you see everyones or just friends chatboxes\n\nI think you should be able to choose who sees YOUR chatbox\n\nEveryone, Friends, Specific Person, Maybe Group based?\n\nALSO\n\nYou should be able to \"mute\"/hide others chatboxes if you don't want to see them like how you can mute an individual or hide their avatar",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-09T09:05:12.690Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, chat boxes default to friends only, and while I'm sure tons of people would like it to default to everyone, I'm willing to bet there's an actual design decision as to why it doesn't.\n\nThe compromise I would like here is that, similar to how nameplates have icons indicating whether someone can interact with your avatar or whether they have muted you, I would like a small icon to indicate when someone cannot see my chat box. Something like a little keyboard with a line crossing it out, similar to how someone who's muted you gets a pair of crossed out headphones.",
